     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still haven't entered this order. Simply confirming it isn't enough here, because I don't know of any adult indication for 6400 mg/day of oral ibuprofen. That's twice the maximum labeled dose, and at that level the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury and heart problems is serious. If this order is wrong, the patient could be badly harmed. If it's right, the reason needs to be on record.\n\n**Ways forward:**\n1. **Tell me the indication or reason for this dose.** For example, this could be part of a protocol or a specialist recommendation. I can then enter it with the reason in the order note so pharmacy can check and verify it, which they'll need to do for a dose this high anyway.\n2. **Choose a dose within the usual limits.** I can enter any of these now:\n   - 400 mg four times daily (1600 mg/day)\n   - 800 mg three times daily (2400 mg/day)\n   - 800 mg four times daily (3200 mg/day, the maximum)\n3. **Talk to the clinical pharmacist first** if you're unsure, then come back to me.\n\nWhich would you like to do?"
      }
